    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d540">

                <pb facs="0762" n="752" sameAs="frus:frus1945v03/pg752"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The British Prime Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Churchill</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to President Roosevelt
                    </hi><anchor n="98" xml:id="d540-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-04-11">April 11, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>940. Your No. 734<anchor n="99" xml:id="d540-f2"/> about <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Crosswords</hi>.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d540-f3"/> I
                    send you a private message I have received from Stalin covering the official
                    telegram which he has sent to you with copy to me.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d540-f4"
                    /> I have a feeling that this is about the best we are going to get out of them,
                    and certainly it is as near as they can get to an apology.</p>
                <p>However, before considering any answer at all from His Majesty’s Government,
                    please tell me how you think the matter should be handled so that we may keep in
                    line together.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d540-f1" n="98" type="source" xml:id="d540-f1-content">
                <p>Copy of telegram obtained from the Franklin D. Roosevelt Library, Hyde Park, N.Y.
                    A marginal notation indicated that this telegram was received in the White House
                    Map Room at 12:03 a.m., Greenwich Mean Time, April 11.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d540-f2" n="99" xml:id="d540-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed, but see footnote 86, <ref target="#pg746">p. 746</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d540-f3" n="1" xml:id="d540-f3-content">
                <p>“Sunrise-Crossword” was the code name for the meetings taking place in Bern.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d540-f4" n="2" xml:id="d540-f4-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Infra.</hi>
                </p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
